  m_Name: CubeLoreSO
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  LoreTitle: The Cube
  Lore: "I. \u201CTo let the world pass me by\u2026\u201D\r\n\r\nDays of static peace
    and stability were endless, and the Cube was wholly content with its peaceful
    stasis in the vast gray dimension. It was a simple life illuminated by directional
    axes\u2019 arrows, a humble camera, and the occasional lagging stutter from a
    crap CPU. Nevertheless, it was fulfilling enough to rest simply among everything,
    and it wasn\u2019t really like the cube could move on its own so it didn\u2019t
    really have a choice, which made its happiness even better. Although, every so
    often, the chilling phantom feeling of an omnipresent gaze would sometimes befall
    it, and the Cube couldn\u2019t help but feel uneasy when the sensation passed.
    Perhaps it was just paranoia, and its peace truly was everlasting. Surely.\r\n\r#\nII.
    \u201CJust what are you making me become\u2026\u201D\r\n\r\nPulling, stretching,
    shaping, the Cube had found its body in a state of sudden change and manipulation.
    It felt the cursor suddenly tug at its body over and over, reshaping and remodeling
    with every CTRL+Z just to end up with a shape that resembled a dilapidated mobius
    strip. Wasn\u2019t it supposed to turn into a donut? With sprinkles? How do you
    mess up a 3D donut into a shape with one side? Regardless, with every amateur
    twist of its body, the Cube found itself yearning for its days of still peace.\r\n\r#\nIII.
    \u201CUnhand me! Or\u2026don\u2019t\u2026\u201D\r\n\r\nThe Cube feared admitting
    it, but its sculptor truly was becoming fluent in their work. In fact, it slowly
    became harder and harder to really name itself as the Cube because it had become
    so many people, animals, plants, and yes, an actual well-shaped donut. The Cube\u2019s
    countless bodies and lives had grown so beautiful and defined that it seemed
    to lose more and more of its fear of the sculptor\u2019s touch, even simmering
    with excitement as to what it could become next. Yes, there was a romanticism
    in laying immobile for countless days on end, but maybe it was really time to
    embrace its new era of modeling.\r\n\r\n\r#\nIV. \u201CI wanted to be your muse,
    forevermore\u2026\u201D\r\n\r\nSeemingly a day like any other, the Cube eyed
    (does it have eyes\u2026?) its sculptor\u2019s cursor as it swung to and fro,
    it seemingly being in a state of thought. What body would they give it today?
    The Cube hummed with excitement as the cursor hovered over it, bracing for its
    first change-\r\n\r\n[X] [Del]\r\n\r#\nV.  \u201CCan a life be returned?\u201D\r\n\r\nWas
    it for a clean workspace? An unattainable shape via cube? Was the Cube itself
    useless? It seethed as it watched on from nowhere, staring as its former sculptor
    drew models from thin air to replace it. Worse, there really was no difference
    in the gorgeous bodies the sculptor blew life into, it simply was now excluding
    the Cube for good, and it could do nothing but watch on as awe-striking figures
    seemed to bloom from the cursor\u2019s touch.\r\n\r\nNo, the Cube could do something.\r\n\r\nSurfaces
    melted into tens into hundreds of polygons as rage boiled in its body, splitting
    and shaping on its own. The desperate desire for revenge gripped at the core
    of the Cube\u2019s soul, speaking into it a newfound, vicious tenacity. Never
    again, would it be deleted and cheated of its peace, its lives, like this. \r\n"
